The expected database behavior is:

| Action              | Booking count | Room status |
| ------------------- | ------------- | ----------- |
| Create room         | 0             | AVAILABLE   |
| Add first booking   | 1             | BOOKED      |
| Add second booking  | 2             | BOOKED      |
| Delete one booking  | 1             | BOOKED      |
| Delete last booking | 0             | AVAILABLE   |

Important: This is a simple learning project. The booking count is maintained by the controller, so don't manually modify it in MongoDB. In a production application, concurrent bookings and database failures require additional safeguards.
